native_sql=[
{'id':'S01','subject':'original journal columns and once-only body','native_predicate':"OLD.operation IS 'v2:session.control'; OLD/NEW principal,project,operation,key,request_hash,status,headers,created_at compare with IS (and typeof plus hex(CAST(... AS BLOB)) for exact bytes); only body differs. CAST(body AS TEXT) must be valid strict JSON input; old ACK/new COMPLETED; never ACK->ACK, final->final even no-op, reverse or unrelated method. Check original retained bytes and exact final bytes.",'limit':'JSON parsing/type subgate does not prove UTF8/JCS/full schema; use CASE to fail closed on invalid JSON and NULL. No WHEN NOT(expr) nullable bypass.'},
{'id':'S02','subject':'CANCEL envelope/response finite outer shapes','native_predicate':'On decoded JSON text: json_type(object); json_each key-set EXACT count9 for envelope and response (required names from frozen schema); every key once; no unknowns. CANCEL payload exact3 action,target_id,reason with string types/action=CANCEL. Command/session/client/project identity strings nonempty; writer_epoch/expected_revision JSON integer>=1. Response protocol/method/command/session match original; ACK PendingResult exact fields; COMPLETED ControlResult exact7 fields, three true booleans and nested snapshot type object; error/error_code must be explicit JSON null, not missing. Nullable fields use json_type IS null-literal vs SQL NULL deliberately.','limit':'Envelope stored in private base64 first needs trusted decode; nested SessionSnapshot has external refs, date-time, arrays and input/read validation differences. Enumerating these outer fields is not full schema.'},
{'id':'S03','subject':'duplicate JSON keys','native_predicate':"After guarded json_valid, traverse json_tree(document); for object parents GROUP BY parent,key HAVING count(*)<>1 for present property groups (detect duplicates count>1); use decoded keys/collation BINARY, including escaped aliases, nested objects. Arrays counted/indexed separately. Exact key membership with json_each.",'limit':'This is a proposed duplicate-key predicate requiring pinned SQLite adversarial tests, not executed here. json_valid alone accepts duplicate names; SQLite normalization/json() is not RFC8785. Unicode surrogate/invalidUTF8 strictness needs Go.'},
{'id':'S04','subject':'private headers','native_predicate':'Header SQLite TEXT, length(CAST(headers AS BLOB))<=1398200; strict outer JSON object exact3 string names schema/encoding/raw_envelope_base64; constants and base64 text length<=1398104. OLD.headers equals NEW.headers exactly and binds original identity locator.','limit':'Current builtins provide neither the approved strict base64 decoder/roundtrip nor ContentHash/JCS/SHA256. Character/padding checks alone cannot establish decoded UTF8 envelope or unused bits. Do not silently parse headers as HTTP headers or allow session.create derived SID for CANCEL.'},
{'id':'S05','subject':'identity and command bindings','native_predicate':'Unique global identity principal+command_id, protocol2, project, method=session.control, operation v2:session.control, request_hash equality with journal and witness. Unique original control_request_id; original SID matches CANCEL SID. Deferred FK locator references original journal. Immutable original scope/client/epoch/revision/target belong admission.','limit':'Equality of same supplied hashes does not recompute original ContentHash; current head/latest Session never repairs a missing original envelope.'},
{'id':'S06','subject':'complete witness group','native_predicate':'Exactly one root ADMITTED and unique typed member rows for complete sorted unique task set; member count/set equality against original pre-mutation Goal-membership query or exact target Run.task_id. Every member has identical principal/project/command/request/group locator; no extra or omitted task via two-way NOT EXISTS. Every FINALIZED member references its exact ADMITTED row and variant identity, no copies from other commands. Phase/root/member cardinality must support Goal including tasks without Session.','limit':'To independently check original complete membership, insert ADMITTED at pre-mutation state, not reconstruct later and not compare only self-reported membership_hash. Historical proof cannot query current active_run_id.'},
{'id':'S07','subject':'Task/Run/dispatch/effect/queue relational anchors','native_predicate':'Join exact domain_versions project/kind/id/revision and typed epoch, Task/Goal original refs, dispatch manifest/key/identity and historical observation artifact ref. At finalization reject any latest resource_effect state PREPARED/STARTED/UNKNOWN, missing/gapped history, changed request/reservation key; latest key determined by exact sequence, not any older terminal row. Original generation must exist when queued; all commands through admitted accepted_through have terminal CONSUMED/DROPPED with complete same-generation receipt chains; required clear/abort/idle facts and native cleanup refs match exact Run/epoch/process; restore_fenced or missing source facts refuse live finalization.','limit':'SQL can test stored rows; it cannot observe OS child cleanup or SDK completion itself, compute missing hashes, or turn an absent generation into evidence. Trusted producers and content validation remain required.'},
{'id':'S08','subject':'DELETE/REPLACE/UPSERT guards','native_predicate':'Protect witness UPDATE/DELETE always; BEFORE INSERT rejects all existing PK AND every unique alternative collision, independent of recursive_triggers. Controls freeze authority/membership/original once set; final_response once only and final state monotonic. Protected original CANCEL journal DELETE rejected; BEFORE INSERT blocks conflicting original PK and protected global principal/command locator. Guard UPSERT UPDATE through same exact transition (and disallow conflict-driven replacement entirely); no INSERT OR IGNORE success interpreted as write. All guards RAISE(ABORT), caller verifies RowsAffected.','limit':'An attacker able to drop triggers or rewrite every trusted anchor is outside in-file consistency guarantees. New guards must cover deletion/replacement of the exact referenced anchor rows, with legitimate monotonic producer updates retained; if required trigger coverage conflicts with original runtime writes, stop and scope the caller, not weaken it.'}]

